// A `forbid` guarded by a provider whose argument is a *nested* principal
// entity attribute (`principal.address.zone`, two segments deep). The
// unconditional `permit` allows Read; the `forbid` blocks it when the
// principal is in a restricted zone.
//
// The forbid shape is the point: if the nested provider argument failed to
// resolve (the pre-fix behaviour, where paths deeper than one segment silently
// became `Null`), the provider would not see "restricted", the forbid would
// not fire, and the request would be **allowed** — a fail-open security hole.
// With nested paths resolving correctly, the forbid fires and the request is
// denied. (Contrast `0020`/`0021`, which use single-segment paths.)

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
);

forbid (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when guardrails {
    Zone::Blocked(principal.address.zone).blocked == true
};
